WEBVTT

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.160
The best way you can contribute
to a secure .Local is

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:06.680
by keeping in mind
the following.

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:13.200
Know how to report: Physical
security will be on the ground,

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:15.205
but if you're not sure
where to find them,

00:00:15.205 --> 00:00:17.365
find the nearest
event staff member.

00:00:17.365 --> 00:00:20.165
You'll get to know them
during volunteer orientation.

00:00:20.165 --> 00:00:23.845
And let them know if you see
anything that raises your suspicion.

00:00:23.845 --> 00:00:26.125
Keep your machine secure.

00:00:26.165 --> 00:00:29.540
.Local is not the time to
leave your laptop lying around.

00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:33.140
Make sure you leave it in your
room or in a spot designated as

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:35.140
secure by the event team.

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:38.180
Keep privileged
information privileged.

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:41.140
Refrain from conversations
involving customer information

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:44.380
or company information
on the conference floor.

00:00:45.015 --> 00:00:47.895
Be aware of social
engineering tactics.

00:00:47.895 --> 00:00:51.255
Malicious actors might try
various methods to gain human

00:00:51.255 --> 00:00:54.055
intelligence, access
to company machines,

00:00:54.055 --> 00:00:56.775
or gain access to
restricted areas.

00:00:56.775 --> 00:01:00.575
Know these tactics and know
when to report these behaviors.